# No upstream refs in usage guidelines

In docs **usage guidelines** (Do / Don't, how-to prose, component mapping rationale, and other instructional copy), never mention Apps SDK, Apps SDK UI, OpenAI, Rogo, or other upstream sources.

Write as **Standard UI**. Name tokens and classes directly (`shadow-lg`, `text-md`, `rounded-xl`).

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — upstream attribution in guidelines
<li>Use shadow-lg for cards, matching Apps SDK elevation 300</li>
<p>Apps SDK examples often combine shadow-lg with a border.</p>

// ✅ GOOD — product-owned guidance
<li>Use shadow-lg for cards, menus, and elevated surfaces</li>
<p>Prefer one clear edge treatment — hairline or border — unless the pattern needs both.</p>
```

Attribution to source systems belongs in the repo README, package READMEs, or internal comments — not in end-user usage guidelines on the docs site.
